  "real": false,
  "story": {
   "title": "Gilgamesh's Tavern",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "kind": "paragraph",
     "text": [
      {
       "text": "The door swings shut behind you, and the chill of the courtyard is gone. Firelight plays across old timbers. Somewhere a lute is being played, not quite in tune, and nobody seems to mind."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "paragraph",
     "text": [
      {
       "text": "Every table is taken. Fighters compare scars while a young mage pretends not to listen. In the gallery above, a priest blesses a bowl of stew, and the thief beside him quietly counts the spoons."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "paragraph",
     "text": [
      {
       "text": "Behind the bar stands a broad, gray-bearded man with his arms folded and a smile that has outlasted a great many customers."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "paragraph",
     "text": [
      {
       "text": "\"Welcome, welcome,\" says "
      },
      {
       "text": "Gilgamesh",
       "bold": true
      },
      {
       "text": ". \"Another one answering Trebor's call, I see. Sit anywhere you like. Not that table, though. It's kept for a party that went down to settle matters with Werdna.\" He polishes a tankard thoughtfully. \"Some while ago now.\""
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "paragraph",
     "text": [
      {
       "text": "He nods toward the crowded room."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "paragraph",
     "text": [
      {
       "text": "\"Everyone here means to go down into the Maze, and the wise ones know better than to go alone. Choose your companions with care. A friend who will carry you home is worth more than gold. A friend who offers to carry your gold is not quite the same thing.\""
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "paragraph",
     "text": [
      {
       "text": "You notice that good and evil seldom share a table for long. Gilgamesh assures you they fare even worse sharing a corridor beneath the castle."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "paragraph",
     "text": [
      {
       "text": "\"Well, then,\" says Gilgamesh, setting down the tankard. \"Find yourself some good company. The Maze will still be there in the morning. It always is.\""
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "challenge",
     "items": [
      [
       {
        "text": "Your adventure begins with good company. Gather your party."
       }
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 },
